    "turns": 30,
    "tool_calls": 30,
    "summary": "Fixed the wchunk package to match the actual binary format found in the sample files. Key changes:\n\n**Format discovery from samples:**\n- Header: 12 bytes = MAGIC(\"WCHK\") + version(u8) + count(u32LE) + reserved(3 zero bytes)\n- Records: Each record has a 4-byte header (tag as u16LE + size as u16LE) followed by `size` payload bytes, then zero-padding to align the total record (header+payload) to an 8-byte boundary\n- Footer: 6 bytes = CRC-32(u32LE, 4 bytes) + tag_sum(u16LE, 2 bytes)\n- CRC covers header + all record bytes (including padding)\n- Tag sum = sum of all record tags mod 65536\n\n**Files modified:**\n\n1. **crc.py**: Changed `compute_crc()` from `zlib.crc32(data) ^ 0xFFFFFFFF` to `zlib.crc32(data) & 0xFFFFFFFF` (standard CRC-32)\n\n2. **header.py**: Changed record count encoding from big-endian (`>I`) to little-endian (`<I`)\n\n3. **codec.py**: Complete rewrite:\n   - Records use fixed-width u16LE fields (not varints) with 8-byte alignment\n   - Footer is 6 bytes (CRC-32 + tag sum), not 4\n  ",
    "changed_workspace": true
  },
